{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "retry-storm",
  "title": "A retry storm",
  "summary": "Retries rescue a brief failure but can turn a slowdown into an outage. See how clients make a struggling database worse, and how to retry politely.",
  "level": "intermediate",
  "minutes": 4,
  "project": {
    "name": "A retry storm",
    "serverProfile": {
      "os": "linux",
      "cpuCores": 4,
      "cpuGhz": 3.0,
      "ramGb": 16.0,
      "disk": {
        "kind": "ssd",
        "iops": 20000
      },
      "network": {
        "bandwidthMbps": 1000.0,
        "latencyMs": 0.5
      },
      "virtualization": "vm",
      "fdLimit": 65536
    },
    "trafficProfile": {
      "concurrentUsers": 1000,
      "requestsPerSecond": 330.0,
      "readRatio": 0.8,
      "spike": {
        "kind": "none"
      }
    },
    "topology": {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "client",
          "kind": "client",
          "label": "Users",
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 120
          },
          "template": null,
          "settings": {},
          "replicas": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "app",
          "kind": "appServer",
          "label": "App server",
          "position": {
            "x": 260,
            "y": 120
          },
          "template": null,
          "settings": {},
          "replicas": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "db",
          "kind": "database",
          "label": "Database",
          "position": {
            "x": 520,
            "y": 120
          },
          "template": null,
          "settings": {},
          "replicas": 1
        }
      ],
      "edges": [
        {
          "id": "e-client-app",
          "source": "client",
          "target": "app"
        },
        {
          "id": "e-app-db",
          "source": "app",
          "target": "db"
        }
      ]
    },
    "chaos": {
      "faults": [],
      "policy": {
        "timeoutMs": 10000.0,
        "maxRetries": 0,
        "backoffMs": 100.0
      }
    },
    "slo": {
      "p95Ms": 200.0,
      "maxErrorRate": 0.01
    }
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Everything is healthy",
      "narration": [
        "A small app talks to its database at 330 requests per second. The app server is fairly busy but coping, and the database is comfortable.",
        "Clients give up after ten seconds and never retry."
      ],
      "highlight": ["db"],
      "changes": [],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 60.0,
        "speed": 8
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The database has a brownout",
      "narration": [
        "For fifteen seconds the database becomes eight times slower, perhaps because of a noisy neighbour. It can no longer keep up with 250 requests per second.",
        "Requests pile up, some are rejected, and latency spikes. Then the slowdown ends and the system recovers."
      ],
      "highlight": ["db"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "addFault",
          "fault": {
            "id": "brownout",
            "target": "db",
            "kind": {
              "kind": "slowdown",
              "factor": 8.0
            },
            "startS": 15.0,
            "durationS": 15.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 60.0,
        "speed": 8
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "errorRateAbove",
          "value": 0.02
        },
        {
          "kind": "recoveryBelowS",
          "value": 3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Clients retry",
      "narration": [
        "Now every failed request is tried again, up to three times, almost immediately. It sounds harmless, and for a brief blip it often helps.",
        "Here it adds load to a database that is already drowning. Retries pile on top of the original requests, so the backlog is bigger and takes much longer to clear: the system needs roughly eight seconds to recover instead of one."
      ],
      "highlight": ["db"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "setPolicy",
          "policy": {
            "timeoutMs": 10000.0,
            "maxRetries": 3,
            "backoffMs": 10.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 60.0,
        "speed": 8
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "recoveryAboveS",
          "value": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Fail fast instead",
      "narration": [
        "Stop retrying and give up after two seconds. During the brownout more requests now fail, but they fail quickly instead of hanging for many seconds.",
        "With no extra load and no hopeless waiting requests, the database recovers within a second or two of the slowdown ending. Failing fast gives a struggling system room to recover."
      ],
      "highlight": ["db"],
      "changes": [
        {
          "kind": "setPolicy",
          "policy": {
            "timeoutMs": 2000.0,
            "maxRetries": 0,
            "backoffMs": 100.0
          }
        }
      ],
      "play": {
        "mode": "live",
        "durationS": 60.0,
        "speed": 8
      },
      "expect": [
        {
          "kind": "meetsTargets",
          "value": false
        },
        {
          "kind": "recoveryBelowS",
          "value": 3
        },
        {
          "kind": "p95BelowMs",
          "value": 3000
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
